cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Data mobilization as the critical bottleneck for bias-aware biodiversity inference"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code measuring the share of GBIF-mediated occurrence records and
  datasets that carry interpretable sampling metadata (eventID,
  parentEventID, samplingProtocol, sampleSizeValue, organismQuantity and
  measurement extensions), by taxonomic group.
authors:
  - family-names: Finstad
    given-names: Anders G.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4529-6266"
    affiliation: >-
      Gjærevoll Centre for Biodiversity Foresight Analyses, and Department of
      Natural History, NTNU University Museum, Norwegian University of Science
      and Technology (NTNU), Trondheim, Norway
repository-code: "https://github.com/andersfi/data-mobilization-as-bottleneck"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - biodiversity
  - GBIF
  - Darwin Core
  - sampling metadata
  - data mobilization
